WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.914
The labor shortage is real, as every

00:00:01.914 --> 00:00:03.876
industry has directly felt the need for

00:00:03.876 --> 00:00:05.788
supporting measures for migrant workers

00:00:05.788 --> 00:00:08.172
. But many people wonder: is this labor

00:00:08.172 --> 00:00:10.347
shortage just about needing low-wage

00:00:10.347 --> 00:00:12.640
workers, or is there a genuine lack of

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:14.933
capacity, making it necessary to bring

00:00:14.933 --> 00:00:17.362
in foreign labor? From that perspective

00:00:17.362 --> 00:00:19.768
, people worry that if migrant worker

00:00:19.768 --> 00:00:22.237
policies are too open, it might hinder

00:00:22.237 --> 00:00:24.326
our AI transformation and reduce

00:00:24.326 --> 00:00:26.795
opportunities for local workers to get

00:00:26.795 --> 00:00:29.349
raises. How do you view this issue?

00:00:29.349 --> 00:00:31.841
>> Our current workforce is indeed

00:00:31.841 --> 00:00:32.954
insufficient.

00:00:32.954 --> 00:00:34.982
>> I am very concerned that this labor

00:00:34.982 --> 00:00:36.785
shortage will affect industrial

00:00:36.785 --> 00:00:37.562
development.

00:00:37.562 --> 00:00:38.562
>> Yes.

00:00:38.562 --> 00:00:40.966
>> So, after I took office, we did a few

00:00:40.966 --> 00:00:43.060
things. First, we continued to open up

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:44.960
access to blue-collar foreign migrant

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:46.606
workers. It’s not just for the

00:00:46.606 --> 00:00:48.421
manufacturing sector. During President

00:00:48.421 --> 00:00:50.015
Tsai’s term, it was expanded to the

00:00:50.015 --> 00:00:51.731
agricultural sector. Now, we have

00:00:51.731 --> 00:00:54.931
expanded it to the service sector.

00:00:54.931 --> 00:00:57.283
>> Even if you have a child under 12 at

00:00:57.283 --> 00:00:59.826
home, you can hire someone to help with

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:01.988
domestic tasks, allowing women or

00:01:01.988 --> 00:01:04.341
homemakers more time to pursue their

00:01:04.341 --> 00:01:08.744
careers. We are continuing to open

00:01:08.744 --> 00:01:10.080
things up.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:12.554
>> Recently, we proposed that any company

00:01:12.554 --> 00:01:14.838
that raises an employee's salary by

00:01:14.838 --> 00:01:17.313
2,000 NTD per month will be granted an

00:01:17.313 --> 00:01:19.407
additional quota, though foreign

00:01:19.407 --> 00:01:21.628
workers cannot exceed half of your

00:01:21.628 --> 00:01:23.124
company's total staff.

00:01:23.124 --> 00:01:24.918
>> So, it benefits local workers on one

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:26.470
hand and helps businesses solve

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:29.523
problems on the other. Yes, exactly.

00:01:29.523 --> 00:01:31.358
Another point is that when I was

00:01:31.358 --> 00:01:33.415
Premier, we promoted the Act for the

00:01:33.415 --> 00:01:35.528
Recruitment and Employment of Foreign

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:37.697
Professionals, and we further expanded

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:39.647
it last December.

00:01:39.647 --> 00:01:41.903
>> This law provides pathways for foreign

00:01:41.903 --> 00:01:44.103
white-collar professionals to come to

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:46.186
Taiwan; the Employment Gold Card is

00:01:46.186 --> 00:01:47.791
based on this legislation.

00:01:47.791 --> 00:01:50.714
>> Now, we have opened it up even further.

00:01:50.714 --> 00:01:53.549
To what extent? It means for foreign

00:01:53.549 --> 00:01:55.334
students. As long as you have a

00:01:55.334 --> 00:01:57.093
master's degree or higher, once you

00:01:57.093 --> 00:01:58.805
graduate, you can stay in Taiwan.

00:01:58.805 --> 00:02:00.613
Previously, you had to leave, but now

00:02:00.613 --> 00:02:02.469
you can stay for at least two years to

00:02:02.469 --> 00:02:04.277
look for work, and if you find a job,

00:02:04.277 --> 00:02:05.805
you can stay with a work visa.

00:02:05.805 --> 00:02:06.798
>> Hmm.

00:02:06.798 --> 00:02:08.195
>> Right, and in the future, we are

00:02:08.195 --> 00:02:09.635
considering whether to grant them

00:02:09.635 --> 00:02:11.160
residency permits once they reach a

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:12.858
certain level. OK, so this leads to the

00:02:12.858 --> 00:02:14.346
question of whether we are gradually

00:02:14.346 --> 00:02:15.875
shifting from a migrant worker policy

00:02:15.875 --> 00:02:17.496
toward an immigration policy. We have

00:02:17.496 --> 00:02:19.227
to admit that for the first six months

00:02:19.227 --> 00:02:20.958
of this year, the number of births—I

00:02:20.958 --> 00:02:22.555
recall it was around 69,000 for the

00:02:22.555 --> 00:02:24.241
first nine months—we might not even

00:02:24.241 --> 00:02:26.041
hit 90,000 for the whole year. With the

00:02:26.041 --> 00:02:27.598
population shrinking so rapidly, does

00:02:27.598 --> 00:02:29.074
this mean our migrant worker policy

00:02:29.074 --> 00:02:30.180
will sooner or later shift

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:31.655
significantly toward an immigration

00:02:31.655 --> 00:02:33.130
policy, and we will begin to accept

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:34.729
more immigrants to fill Taiwan's labor

00:02:34.729 --> 00:02:35.075
force?

00:02:35.075 --> 00:02:37.246
>> Yes, when I was Premier, I proposed a

00:02:37.246 --> 00:02:40.073
New Economic Immigration Act. Mm.

00:02:40.073 --> 00:02:41.682
>> It means that based on the human

00:02:41.682 --> 00:02:43.536
resources required by our industries,

00:02:43.536 --> 00:02:45.539
we will hire these foreign individuals.

00:02:45.539 --> 00:02:47.502
>> Whether blue-collar or white-collar,

00:02:47.502 --> 00:02:49.413
once they arrive and meet a certain

00:02:49.413 --> 00:02:50.999
standard, we can grant them.

00:02:50.999 --> 00:02:53.431
>> This residence permit, a residence

00:02:53.431 --> 00:02:54.018
permit.

00:02:54.018 --> 00:02:57.332
>> Granting residence permits is more...in

00:02:57.332 --> 00:03:01.332
society...
